# nloops [1] parses and allocates fine; nverts's entry, 4.5, is not an
# integer, so TokenVector::toRtIntVector() throws while building the second
# array. The already-built nloops array must not leak across that throw.
# This is a genuine token-level syntax error (RIE_SYNTAX), not one of this
# request's own softer structural checks, so it aborts the file: unlike the
# other malformed fixtures here, the trailing Sphere is never reached.
Display "malformed_out.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.6]
Surface "matte" "Ka" [1] "Kd" [0]
AttributeBegin
	PointsGeneralPolygons [1] [4.5] [0 1 2 3]
		"P" [-1 -1 0  1 -1 0  1 1 0  -1 1 0]
AttributeEnd
AttributeBegin
	Translate 2 0 0
	Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
